In one line:

YAML is a simple text file used to tell tools and platforms what steps and configuration they should follow.

For example, in CI/CD, the YAML file acts like an instruction sheet: when code is pushed → what to build → what to test → where to deploy.

In CI/CD, YAML defines the workflow steps, so 
a complete GitHub Actions YAML file that builds your FastAPI image and deploys it to Cloud Run turns the instruction sheet into an executable deployment pipeline.

